{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014EFf81TpCp8VBKQPa2qngn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities have no formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation diverge in edge-case behavior. This project derives formal specs (SRDs) from C source, generates Go implementations via an AI orchestrator, and verifies parity via differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** SRDs in `docs/specs/` → orchestrator generates code in `cmd/<util>/main.go` → differential tests in `<util>_test.go` via `pkg/testutils` compare against `g<util>` reference binaries. Shared libraries: `pkg/sys` (syscalls), `pkg/format` (output formatting), `pkg/hashutil`, `pkg/sizeparse`, `pkg/encutil`.\n\n**Implementation status:**\n- Implemented: pkg/sys, pkg/hashutil, pkg/sizeparse, pkg/encutil, magefiles, cmd/sponge, cmd/true, cmd/false, cmd/yes, cmd/basename, cmd/dirname\n- Not started (no code): pkg/format, pkg/testutils, and 100+ cmd/ utilities\n- All 114 SRDs are spec_complete with requirements \"ready\" in requirement_states\n\n**Current release priority:**\n- rel00.0: format and testutils not started, but their SRDs are NOT in requirement_states — cannot propose\n- rel01.1 (cat): SRD not in requirement_states — cannot propose\n- rel01.2 (sponge): already implemented\n- **rel01.3 (du)**: srd009-du has all 19 requirements \"ready\", code \"not started\" — first target\n- rel02.0: all 5 utilities implemented\n\n## Weight Budget Analysis\n\nAssuming default weight=1 for all srd009-du sub-requirements (weights not provided in context):\n\n```\nTask 0: R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: R1.5(w=1) + R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: R2.4(w=1) + R2.5(w=1) + R2.6(w=1) + R2.7(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: R2.8(w=1) + R3.1(w=1) + R3.2(w=1) + R3.3(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\nRemaining for next batch: R4.1, R4.2, R5.1 (3 requirements).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/du: recursive traversal and default output (srd009-du R1.1-R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd009-du.yaml (requirements R1.1 through R1.4)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (FileInfo struct and Stat/Lstat functions for file metadata)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: du utility -- recursive directory disk usage reporting\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement basic recursive directory traversal and disk usage summation per srd009-du R1.1\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement default output format with tab-separated block count and pathname per srd009-du R1.2\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement block size calculation and default allocation units per srd009-du R1.3\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement hard link deduplication so shared blocks are counted once per srd009-du R1.4\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per the shared SIGPIPE protocol\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use pkg/sys.Lstat for file metadata to avoid following symlinks by default\n      - id: D3\n        text: Use the standard flag package for command-line option parsing\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build -o bin/du ./cmd/du/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./cmd/du/ passes with no warnings\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Binary recursively reports disk usage for directories per srd009-du R1.1-R1.4\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Default output uses tab-separated block count and path, one line per directory entry\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/du: summarize, all-files, and total modes (srd009-du R1.5, R2.1-R2.3)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd009-du.yaml (requirements R1.5, R2.1 through R2.3)\n      - cmd/du/main.go (existing implementation with core traversal from previous task)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add exit code handling, summarize, all-files, and grand total modes\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement exit code and error reporting behavior per srd009-du R1.5\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement summarize mode (-s) reporting only the total for each argument per srd009-du R2.1\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement all-files mode (-a) reporting usage for every file per srd009-du R2.2\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement grand total mode (-c) printing a cumulative total line per srd009-du R2.3\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Wire -s, -a, and -c flags via the standard flag package consistent with existing flags\n      - id: D2\n        text: Exit code 1 on any error per GNU du convention, continuing to process remaining arguments\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build -o bin/du ./cmd/du/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./cmd/du/ passes with no warnings\n      - id: AC3\n        text: du -s outputs exactly one line per argument with the total size\n      - id: AC4\n        text: du -c appends a grand total line after all argument output\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/du: depth limit, filesystem boundary, symlinks, and exclusion (srd009-du R2.4-R2.7)\"\n  dependency: 1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd009-du.yaml (requirements R2.4 through R2.7)\n      - cmd/du/main.go (existing implementation from previous tasks)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (FileInfo.Dev field for filesystem boundary detection)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add traversal control flags -- depth limit, filesystem boundary, symlinks, exclusion\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement max depth limit (-d/--max-depth) restricting output to N levels per srd009-du R2.4\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement one-filesystem mode (-x/--one-file-system) staying on the initial device per srd009-du R2.5\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement dereference mode (-L/--dereference) following symbolic links per srd009-du R2.6\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement exclude patterns (--exclude) skipping files matching the pattern per srd009-du R2.7\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Track the root device ID from pkg/sys.FileInfo.Dev to implement -x filesystem boundary\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use filepath.Match for --exclude pattern matching consistent with GNU du glob semantics\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build -o bin/du ./cmd/du/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./cmd/du/ passes with no warnings\n      - id: AC3\n        text: du -d 1 limits output to one level below the argument\n      - id: AC4\n        text: du -x does not cross filesystem mount points\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/du: apparent size, human-readable output, and null termination (srd009-du R2.8, R3.1-R3.3)\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd009-du.yaml (requirements R2.8, R3.1 through R3.3)\n      - cmd/du/main.go (existing implementation from previous tasks)\n      - pkg/format/format.go (HumanSize and HumanSizeOpts for human-readable output)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add apparent size, human-readable output, SI units, and null-terminated output\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement apparent size mode (--apparent-size) reporting byte counts instead of disk blocks per srd009-du R2.8\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement human-readable output (-h) using binary K/M/G/T suffixes per srd009-du R3.1\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement SI output (--si) using 1000-based unit suffixes per srd009-du R3.2\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement null-terminated output (-0/--null) for machine-parseable output per srd009-du R3.3\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Use pkg/format.HumanSize with Binary=true for -h and Binary=false for --si\n      - id: D2\n        text: Replace newline with null byte for -0 flag at the output formatting layer\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build -o bin/du ./cmd/du/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./cmd/du/ passes with no warnings\n      - id: AC3\n        text: du -h prints sizes with binary suffixes (K, M, G, T)\n      - id: AC4\n        text: du -0 separates entries with null bytes instead of newlines\n```\n\n**Coverage:** 16 of 19 srd009-du requirements across 4 tasks. Remaining R4.1, R4.2, R5.1 (likely version/help/edge cases) deferred to the next batch. Tests for du will also be proposed after implementation tasks complete, consistent with the rule to split implementation and tests."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59280,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59280},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1f7a819-4bc5-4914-a53b-1bb388bef7c0","uuid":"dd2fa4dc-94da-4cea-a8ed-af03c8ef2877"}
